			"Message": "feat(Vine): Populate Server module with constants, helpers, and notification atoms\n\nReplace the intentionally-empty `Source/Server/mod.rs` placeholder with the canonical server-side scaffolding extracted from Mountain's in-tree Vine module. Add `Constants` (default ports, timeouts, message-size cap), `ValidateSocketAddress` (pre-flight parsing and privileged-port warning), `SpawnBindTask` (detached `tokio::spawn` with uniform dev-log instrumentation), and `SpawnBindTaskWithShutdown` (graceful-shutdown variant for daemon embedders like Air). Introduce the `Notification` submodule with `RelayToSky` support and nine pure renderer-event relay atoms (`OutputAppend`, `OutputClear`, `OutputCreate`, `OutputDispose`, `OutputShow`, `OutputChannelClear`, `OutputChannelDispose`, `OutputChannelShow`, `ProgressComplete`). Regenerate `Source/Generated/vine.rs` from `Proto/Vine.proto` so the crate compiles with real protobuf types. Apply rustfmt to `Source/Client/mod.rs`, `Source/Error.rs`, `Source/Host.rs`, `Source/Library.rs`, and `Source/Multiplexer.rs` for consistent line-wrapping.\n\nThis continues Phase 2 of the Mountain-Crate-Split plan: the Vine crate now has both a functional client surface (from the initial bootstrap) and a functional server surface, so Mountain and Air can begin consuming it instead of their in-tree modules.",
			"SHA": "ed69779327946fb821fb124b3582135da75d02c8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T09:33:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⡏⠀",
				40,
				29
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Bootstrap standalone gRPC protocol crate from Mountain in-tree module\n\nSynthesize the Vine crate as an independent repository under `Land/Element/Vine/` per Track-B task #1 of `.hermes/plan/Mountain-Crate-Split.md`. The crate now compiles standalone and exposes the canonical IPC surface for Mountain, Cocoon, and Air.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `Cargo.toml` — workspace-driven dependency set with three cargo features (`client`, `server`, `multiplexer`).\n- `Proto/Vine.proto` — authoritative gRPC schema with bidirectional `Envelope` streaming (OpenChannelFromCocoon / OpenChannelFromMountain) and the full LSP-shaped extension-host surface (hover, completion, definition, references, code actions, formatting, semantic tokens, inlay hints, inline completions, debug, terminal, etc.).\n- `Source/Library.rs` — crate root re-exporting `Error`, `Host`, `Generated`, `Client`, `Server`, and `Multiplexer` modules.\n- `Source/Error.rs` — `VineError` enum with connection, RPC, serialization, transport, and internal error variants and bidirectional `From` impls for `tonic::Status`, `serde_json::Error`, `tonic::transport::Error`, `http::uri::InvalidUri`, and `std::net::AddrParseError`.\n- `Source/Host.rs` — `VineHost` embedder seam plus `IPCProvider` and `ApplicationStateAccess` forward-compatible traits so Mountain, Air, and future Rust Cocoon clients share the same handler surface.\n- `Source/Generated/` — `tonic_prost_build` output module. `vine.rs` is a placeholder regenerated by `build.rs`.\n- `Source/Client/` — fourteen atomized entry points synthesized from `Mountain/Source/Vine/Client/`:\n  - `Shared.rs` — connection pool, per-sidecar metadata, `tokio::sync::broadcast` fan-out, shutdown flag, and message-size validation.\n  - `ConnectToSideCar.rs` / `DisconnectFromSideCar.rs` / `TryConnectSingle.rs` — exponential-backoff connection lifecycle with h2 transport tuning (4 MB stream / 16 MB connection windows, `LAND_TONIC_TUNED`).\n  - `IsClientConnected.rs` / `WaitForClientConnection.rs` — boot-race-friendly readiness checks via `tokio::sync::Notify`.\n  - `CheckSideCarHealth.rs` — pool + metadata health summary.\n  - `SendRequest.rs` / `SendNotification.rs` — wire dispatch with optional streaming-multiplexer fast path when `LAND_VINE_STREAMING=1` and the `multiplexer` feature are enabled.\n  - `SendRequest.rs` — enforces per-call timeout (default 5 000 ms, cap 15 000 ms), atomic-counter request IDs, and structured `VineError::RequestTimeout` / `RequestCanceled` propagation.\n  - `PublishNotification.rs` / `NotificationFrame.rs` / `SubscribeNotifications.rs` / `SubscriberCount.rs` — broadcast fan-out for Effect-TS fibers, OTel emitters, and diagnostic consumers.\n  - `IsShuttingDown.rs` / `MarkShutdown.rs` — global shutdown flag for graceful sidecar teardown.\n- `Source/Multiplexer.rs` — LAND-PATCH B7-S6 P14.1 skeleton: `Open`, `Lookup`, `Notify`, `Request`, and `Cancel` on a per-sidecar bidirectional h2 stream with correlation-ID routing, `oneshot` response parking, and a `tokio::spawn` read pump that fans out notifications to the process-wide broadcast and resolves pending requests. Reverse-RPC request dispatch and cancellation are TODO for P14.1.1 / P14.1.2.\n- `Source/Server/mod.rs` — intentionally empty placeholder; populated in Phase 2.\n- `Source/DevLog.rs` — tag-gated `dev_log!` macro with `LAND_DEV_LOG` filter and `NowNano` monotonic timestamp.\n- `build.rs` — `tonic_prost_build` invocation mirroring Mountain's generation flags.\n- `LICENSE` — CC0 1.0 Universal.\n\nMountain's in-tree `Source/Vine/` remains the production code path until Phase 2 (consumer migration) lands. This commit targets `Element/Vine` exclusively.",
