			"Message": "docs(Vine): Expand Mermaid diagram with detailed RPC methods and implementation structure\n\nReplace the previous high-level Mermaid graph with a substantially more detailed diagram that maps the complete gRPC contract layer. The new diagram includes:\n\n- Explicit MountainService and CocoonService definitions listing all RPC methods (ProcessCocoonRequest, SendCocoonNotification, CancelOperation, and streaming OpenChannel variants)\n- Mountain server-side implementation structure showing the tonic gRPC server, envelope Multiplexer.rs, Client.rs for Mountain-to-Cocoon calls, and Generated/prost bindings\n- Cocoon client-side implementation referencing Services/Mountain/gRPC/Client.ts and Services/gRPC/Server/\n- Grove planned Transport/gRPCTransport as a future WASM host consumer\n- Dashed-line `.defines.` relationships from the protocol spec to implementations\n- Refined color scheme with distinct fill colors for each component role and dashed proto definition nodes\n\nThis provides developers with an at-a-glance reference for how Vine.proto contracts map to concrete Rust and TypeScript implementation paths, improving onboarding clarity for new contributors to the Land IPC layer.",
